IMPORT AND DAMAGE
Use alpha blending, not additive blending. Keep all frames at equal pixels-per-unit and the supplied fixed pivot.
Use Clamp, disable mipmaps unless the engine setup deliberately handles atlas gutters, and avoid sprite auto-trim/re-center.
Pivot: [174, 390] pixels from top left; normalized [0.169922, 0.553977].
Apply damage exactly once, when entering impact frame 08. Do not damage during telegraph or fading debris.
The full indicated footprint is damaged at the impact event.
Approximate footprint is derived from the registered source telegraph. Proposed world dimensions: length_m=16, width_m=1.8.
World footprint and collision must be verified in-engine. These values are authoring guides, not engine-tested settings.

REGISTRATION AND SOURCE INTEGRITY
16 genuinely distinct generated drawings; no tweening, synthetic redraws, scaling, warping or alpha modification.
The persistent lance-lane far tip determines ground center y through impact. The left origin determines the small horizontal registration. Recovery uses the corresponding source-row anchor established at impact; drifting strips are never re-centered.
Each native crop, nominal origin and integer translation is recorded in animation.json.
Where source art crosses a nominal 2x2 divider, the cut moves into the actual empty gap without changing the drawing.
Alpha >=16 was used only for inspection; all faint alpha is preserved. Transparent padding provides real outer gutters.
Raw sources remain separately archived; their hashes are in animation.json. No prompts or internal instructions are included.

DIRECTIONAL REUSE
Horizontal mirror is supported if sprite, pivot and footprint are all mirrored together.
Keep the ground projection upright. Do not vertically flip or arbitrarily rotate the flat image in screen space;
use ground-plane projection or separately authored direction variants instead.

REVIEW
Technical validation is recorded in qa.json. The art remains a generated prototype and has not been integrated into the game.
